<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese 10 month car sales up 6.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese 10 month car sales up 6.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers</p>
<p>Association (ACAP) announced the following new car</p>
<p>registrations:</p>
<p>October 1996 16,319  vs  13,638 (up 19.7 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/Oct 1996 181,995 vs 170,300 (up 6.9 pct)</p>
<p>First 10 months by manufacturers market share (percentage in</p>
<p>brackets), comparative figures refer to same period 1995:</p>
<p>    Fiat	    26,848 (14.75) vs 26,808 (15.74)</p>
<p>    Opel	    26,254 (14.43) vs 26,704 (15.68)</p>
<p>    Renault	 23,089 (12.69) vs 22,338 (13.12)</p>
<p>    Ford	    17,999 ( 9.89) vs 14,479 ( 8.50)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen    14,809 ( 8.14) vs 12,657 ( 7.43)</p>
<p>    Peugeot	 11,780 ( 6.47) vs 12,642 ( 7.42)</p>
<p>    Citroen	 10,914 ( 6.00) vs  8,917 ( 5.24)</p>
<p>    Rover	    7,125 ( 3.91) vs  5,097 ( 2.99)</p>
<p>    Honda	    6,317 ( 3.47) vs  6,005 ( 3.53)</p>
<p>    Seat	     5,844 ( 3.21) vs  7,464 ( 4.38)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
